<title>GERMANY: Bundesbank sets 14-day repo tender.</title>
<headline>Bundesbank sets 14-day repo tender.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank said on Tuedsay it was setting a 14-day securities repurchase tender, offering banks liquidity at a fixed rate of three percent.</p>
<p>Funds will be credited to accounts tomorrow and the securities have to be repurchased on July 9.</p>
<p>A 63.00 billion mark facility, also set at a fixed three percent rate, expires on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A 14-day facility set last week was also fixed at three percent, the rate which has prevailed since August 1996.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
